  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Banker puts up a fixed stake. Each player in turn may bet up to half the current pot without seeing their cards or the dealer's card. Dealer burns one card then turns up one card; player's three cards are exposed. If the player has a higher card of the same suit as the dealer's card, the player is paid twice the bet from the pot; otherwise the bet is added to the pot. If the pot is busted, deal passes. When the pot reaches at least three times its initial size, the dealer may declare a stitch round (final deal) and then keep any remainder; deal then passes left.",
    Player: "Banker puts up a fixed stake. Each player in turn may bet up to half the current pot without seeing their cards or the dealer's card. Dealer burns one card then turns up one card; player's three cards are exposed. If the player has a higher card of the same suit as the dealer's card, the player is paid twice the bet from the pot; otherwise the bet is added to the pot. If the pot is busted, deal passes. When the pot reaches at least three times its initial size, the dealer may declare a stitch round (final deal) and then keep any remainder; deal then passes left.",
    objective: "Players bet that they hold a card of the same suit as and higher than the card the dealer will turn up; they do not see their own cards or the dealer's card before betting. Winner is paid twice the bet from the pot; otherwise the bet goes to the pot.",
    gameplay: "Banker puts up a fixed stake. Each player in turn may bet up to half the current pot without seeing their cards or the dealer's card. Dealer burns one card then turns up one card; player's three cards are exposed. If the player has a higher card of the same suit as the dealer's card, the player is paid twice the bet from the pot; otherwise the bet is added to the pot. If the pot is busted, deal passes. When the pot reaches at least three times its initial size, the dealer may declare a stitch round (final deal) and then keep any remainder; deal then passes left.",
    keyRules: [
      'No one sees cards before bet',
